@startuml geo-cell-write
title US-12: Geo-Cell Write - H3 Cell Computed at Ingest and Stored as Partition Key

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nposition.normalized" as Kafka
participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer
database "TimescaleDB\nposition_history" as TSDB

Kafka -> Consumer : consume event\n{ entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms }

Consumer -> Consumer : compute H3 cell ID\nh3.latLngToCell(lat, lon, resolution=5)

note over Consumer
  H3 resolution 5 = ~252 km² per cell.
  High-traffic areas span multiple cells
  naturally - no single cell becomes
  a write hot-spot.
end note

Consumer -> TSDB : INSERT INTO position_history\n(\n  entity_id,\n  geo_cell,        -- H3 cell ID\n  time_bucket,     -- truncated to chunk interval\n  timestamp_ms,\n  lat, lon, altitude\n)\nON CONFLICT (entity_id, timestamp_ms) DO NOTHING

note over TSDB
  Composite partition key: (geo_cell, time_bucket).
  TimescaleDB routes the row to the chunk
  that owns this geo-cell + time-bucket pair.
  Spatially nearby events land in the same chunk.
end note

@enduml
